Prior art
---------

Distalker's Stalker portal protocol implementation (stalker_api.py) is a Python
reimplementation informed by stalkerhek, a Stalker portal proxy written in Go:

  * https://github.com/erkexzcx/stalkerhek -- the original, now archived,
    distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.
  * https://github.com/kidpoleon/stalkerhek -- a later continuation,
    Copyright (C) 2025 kidpoleon <kidpoleon@proton.me>, distributed under the
    GNU General Public License v3 or later.

The LICENSE file shipped with Distalker 0.9.1 described both as MIT. That was
an error of fact, corrected here: both are GPL-3.0.

Section 13 of the GNU GPL v3 grants permission to combine a GPL-covered work
with a work licensed under the GNU Affero GPL v3, which is what the choice of
AGPL-3.0-only makes possible here. Whatever in stalker_api.py is owed to
stalkerhek therefore travels under terms compatible with the licence of the
work as a whole, and this attribution is preserved in every copy.
